{"parentUuid":null,"isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3c49824ef52b2cb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"调研 OR-Tools CP-SAT 是否提供「自定义 C++ propagator extension」公开 API（而不是 IPASIR-UP），让用户在 OR-Tools 内部加自定义传播器。\n\n## 项目背景\n\n终末地工业规划器 exact LBBD 求解器，主 solver OR-Tools CP-SAT 9.15。当前已 land 多项 CP-SAT 内部钩子用法（add_hint / set parameters / 自定义 cut）。\n\n希望了解的是：**OR-Tools 是否暴露 C++ 级 propagator extension API**，让我们在 OR-Tools 进程内部插入自定义传播器（不是 IPASIR-UP 的进程外）。这样如果某个项目特异约束（比如玩家 hint 类的 storage_box overload separation）能从\"用 add_hint 软提示\"升级到\"硬性传播器\"。\n\n## 上次调研\n\nR1 `abd7846675c5e14fb` 调研过 CaDiCaL Learner API + IPASIR（外部接口，非 C++ extension）。\nR2 `a89b891b3e3123556` 调研过 IPASIR-UP API + PySAT path（外部进程通信）。\nR6 `a656b69d449b928b7` 调研过 OR-Tools main branch undocumented，但没专门看 C++ propagator extension。\n\n**没专门调研过：OR-Tools 自家是否提供 propagator plugin API（C++ subclass interface）**。\n\n## 调研任务\n\n**用 WebSearch / WebFetch 查 OR-Tools GitHub source + dev mailing list / issue tracker**：\n\n1. **C++ propagator extension API**:\n   - 查 ortools/sat/cp_model_solver.cc / ortools/sat/sat_solver.cc / ortools/sat/integer.h\n   - 是否有 abstract Propagator base class 公开\n   - 是否能在 model build 阶段把自定义 Propagator 注册进去\n   - 已有的 propagator 例（element / circuit / no_overlap_2d / cumulative）的实现风格\n\n2. **半官方支持等级**:\n   - OR-Tools docs 是否提到 custom propagator extension\n   - GitHub issue tracker 搜索 \"custom propagator\" / \"propagator extension\" / \"propagator API\" 看用户问的回复\n   - Perron / Furnon 团队的官方表态\n\n3. **替代路径**:\n   - 如果 C++ extension 不公开，能否通过 fork OR-Tools + patch 内部 propagator 列表实现（成本估算）\n   - 跟 IPASIR-UP（进程外 / 单核 SAT 子求解器）相比，C++ extension 的优势\n\n4. **PySAT / CPMpy 替代选项**:\n   - 如果 OR-Tools 没有，PySAT / CPMpy 是否提供同等抽象（用户 Python class 实现 propagator，运行时 callback）\n\n## 输出格式（不超过 600 字，中文）\n\n```\n## OR-Tools CP-SAT C++ propagator extension API\n- 公开 API 状态: 公开 / undocumented / 无\n- 关键 source 文件 + 行号 (如果有)\n- 例子 / 文档\n\n## 实施路径\n- 公开 API → 工时估算（项目自己 +1 propagator）\n- 私有 API → fork patch 路径（成本/风险/维护）\n- 无 → IPASIR-UP / PySAT / CPMpy 替代\n\n## 跟项目契合\n- 适用场景: [storage_box overload / bridge_hop / 其他]\n- 工时: [天/周]\n- ROI: 高/中/低\n\n## verdict\n- 路线图新增条目: 是 / 否\n- 优先级: P1 / P2 / P3 / Excluded\n- 推荐: [具体动作]\n```\n\n## 操作准则\n\n- 必须 WebSearch / WebFetch OR-Tools GitHub 实际代码\n- 必须搜 GitHub issue tracker 关键词\n- 不要凭训练数据猜 API 状态\n- 简洁\n\n开始。"},"uuid":"81f7af9e-e175-49a4-92c1-780e4a3bb37b","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:02.844Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"81f7af9e-e175-49a4-92c1-780e4a3bb37b","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3c49824ef52b2cb9","attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_delta","addedNames":["CronCreate","CronDelete","CronList","EnterWorktree","ExitWorktree","Monitor","NotebookEdit","PushNotification","RemoteTrigger","TaskCreate","TaskGet","TaskList","TaskStop","TaskUpdate","WebFetch","WebSearch"],"addedLines":["CronCreate","CronDelete","CronList","EnterWorktree","ExitWorktree","Monitor","NotebookEdit","PushNotification","RemoteTrigger","TaskCreate","TaskGet","TaskList","TaskStop","TaskUpdate","WebFetch","WebSearch"],"removedNames":[],"readdedNames":[]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8fb349ae-659e-4591-a0e4-e6f6c2243f5e","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:02.846Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8fb349ae-659e-4591-a0e4-e6f6c2243f5e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a3c49824ef52b2cb9","attachment":{"type":"skill_listing","content":"- update-config: Use this skill to configure the Claude Code harness via settings.json. Automated behaviors (\"from now on when X\", \"each time X\", \"whenever X\", \"before/after X\") require hooks configured in settings.json - the harness executes these, not Claude, so memory/preferences cannot fulfill them. Also use for: permissions (\"allow X\", \"add permission\", \"move permission to\"), env vars (\"set X=Y\"), hook troubleshooting, or any changes to settings.json/settings.local.json files. Examples: \"allow npm commands\", \"add bq permission to global settings\", \"move permission to user settings\", \"set DEBUG=true\", \"when claude stops show X\". For simple settings like theme/model, suggest the /config command.\n- keybindings-help: Use when the user wants to customize keyboard shortcuts, rebind keys, add chord bindings, or modify ~/.claude/keybindings.json. Examples: \"rebind ctrl+s\", \"add a chord shortcut\", \"change the submit key\", \"customize keybindings\".\n- simplify: Review changed code for reuse, quality, and efficiency, then fix any issues found.\n- fewer-permission-prompts: Scan your transcripts for common read-only Bash and MCP tool calls, then add a prioritized allowlist to project .claude/settings.json to reduce permission prompts.\n- loop: Run a prompt or slash command on a recurring interval (e.g. /loop 5m /foo). Omit the interval to let the model self-pace. - When the user wants to set up a recurring task, poll for status, or run something repeatedly on an interval (e.g. \"check the deploy every 5 minutes\", \"keep running /babysit-prs\"). Do NOT invoke for one-off tasks.\n- schedule: Create, update, list, or run scheduled remote agents (routines) that execute on a cron schedule. - When the user wants to schedule a recurring remote agent, set up automated tasks, create a cron job for Claude Code, or manage their scheduled agents/routines. Also use when the user wants a one-time scheduled run (\"run this once at 3pm\", \"remind me to check X tomorrow\").\n- claude-api: Build, debug, and optimize Claude API / Anthropic SDK apps. Apps built with this skill should include prompt caching. Also handles migrating existing Claude API code between Claude model versions (4.5 → 4.6, 4.6 → 4.7, retired-model replacements).\nTRIGGER when: code imports `anthropic`/`@anthropic-ai/sdk`; user asks for the Claude API, Anthropic SDK, or Managed Agents; user adds/modifies/tunes a Claude feature (caching, thinking, compaction, tool use, batch, files, citations, memory) or model (Opus/Sonnet/Haiku) in a file; questions about prompt caching / cache hit rate in an Anthropic SDK project.\nSKIP: file imports `openai`/other-provider SDK, filename like `*-openai.py`/`*-generic.py`, provider-neutral code, general programming/ML.\n- init: Initialize a new CLAUDE.md file with codebase documentation\n- review: Review a pull request\n- security-review: Complete a security review of the pending changes on the current branch","skillCount":10,"isInitial":true},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4e2e554f-f6db-45b2-afa7-ab3f6cbb0239","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:02.846Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
