{"parentUuid":"f325e0e4-0706-4d89-9e0d-b788e62cb997","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3c49824ef52b2cb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WhXH8i5YpYQpfT1rGD4Yp6","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"or-tools \"PropagatorInterface\" \"RegisterWith\" GenericLiteralWatcher external user\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"or-tools/ortools/sat/cp_constraints.h at main · google/or-tools\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/blob/main/ortools/sat/cp_constraints.h\"},{\"title\":\"GenericLiteralWatcher | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/sat/integer/GenericLiteralWatcher\"},{\"title\":\"PropagatorInterface | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/sat/integer/PropagatorInterface\"},{\"title\":\"Propagation – Orekit\",\"url\":\"https://www.orekit.org/site-orekit-latest/architecture/propagation.html\"},{\"title\":\"Orekit – Propagation\",\"url\":\"https://www.orekit.org/site-orekit-11.0/architecture/propagation.html\"},{\"title\":\"Uses of Interface org.orekit.propagation.Propagator (OREKIT 13.1.2 API)\",\"url\":\"https://www.orekit.org/static/apidocs/org/orekit/propagation/class-use/Propagator.html\"},{\"title\":\"custom propagator needed ? · google/or-tools · Discussion #3303\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/or-tools/discussions/3303\"},{\"title\":\"CircuitCoveringPropagator | OR-Tools | Google for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://developers.google.com/optimization/reference/sat/circuit/CircuitCoveringPropagator\"},{\"title\":\"Propagator (ORbit Extrapolation KIT 10.2 API)\",\"url\":\"https://www.orekit.org/site-orekit-10.2/apidocs/org/orekit/propagation/Propagator.html\"},{\"title\":\"Propagator (OREKIT 12.2.1 API)\",\"url\":\"https://www.orekit.org/static/apidocs/org/orekit/propagation/Propagator.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found relevant information about OR-Tools' `PropagatorInterface`, `RegisterWith`, and `GenericLiteralWatcher`:\n\nThe `GreaterThanAtLeastOneOfPropagator` class, which inherits from `PropagatorInterface`, includes a method `void RegisterWith(GenericLiteralWatcher* watcher)`. Similarly, the `BooleanXorPropagator` class has a private method `int RegisterWith(GenericLiteralWatcher* watcher)`.\n\nThese are examples from the OR-Tools constraint programming solver showing how propagator classes implement the pattern of registering themselves with a `GenericLiteralWatcher` for constraint propagation. The `RegisterWith` method allows propagators to register their watched variables and behavior with the watcher system.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"6b275bd5-b6c9-42d9-8d9e-fee20b11bc4e","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:36.905Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f325e0e4-0706-4d89-9e0d-b788e62cb997","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"30358365-62af-4aff-927a-7f2a66d67516","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3c49824ef52b2cb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013u7nv75mGnMmFJbJFWo8P5","type":"tool_result","content":"# PropagatorInterface Base Class\n\nBased on the provided content from `ortools/sat/integer.h`, I can identify key information about propagators, though the complete `PropagatorInterface` definition isn't fully visible in this excerpt.\n\n## What's Shown\n\nThe file demonstrates that **`IntegerTrail` implements `SatPropagator`**:\n\n```cpp\nclass IntegerTrail final : public SatPropagator {\n```\n\n## Virtual Methods Visible\n\nThe `IntegerTrail` class overrides these propagator methods:\n\n```cpp\nbool Propagate(Trail* trail) final;\nvoid Untrail(const Trail& trail, int literal_trail_index) final;\nabsl::Span<const Literal> Reason(const Trail& trail, int trail_index,\n                                 int64_t conflict_id) const final;\n```\n\n## Registration Pattern\n\nThe comment indicates propagators self-register:\n\n```cpp\nmodel->GetOrCreate<SatSolver>()->AddPropagator(this);\n```\n\nThis occurs in `IntegerTrail`'s constructor, showing how propagators register with the solver framework.\n\n## Namespace\n\n```cpp\nnamespace operations_research {\nnamespace sat {\n```\n\n**Note:** The full `PropagatorInterface` or `SatPropagator` base class definition isn't included in this file excerpt, so complete details on all virtual methods and registration mechanisms would require viewing the base class header file."}]},"uuid":"17a2a00d-9144-492a-a21d-054744b39d76","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:37.567Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"30358365-62af-4aff-927a-7f2a66d67516","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"8875b875-bedd-49c1-91f2-072724160918","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"64d71192-3b1b-4e70-aef9-d69f40568796","agentId":"a3c49824ef52b2cb9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016N8mHarvQUrdjNnLBX2aFK","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CPMpy custom propagator user defined constraint callback\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Modeling and solving with CPMpy — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/modeling.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy ortools interface (cpmpy.solvers.ortools) — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/feature-check_infeasible_constraints/api/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy: Constraint Programming and Modeling in Python — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/latest/\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy.solvers.ortools — CPMpy 0.9.24 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/extra-require/_modules/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy/docs/modeling.md at master · CPMpy/cpmpy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy/blob/master/docs/modeling.md\"},{\"title\":\"CPMpy ortools interface (cpmpy.solvers.ortools) — CPMpy 0.9.23 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://cpmpy.readthedocs.io/en/cpm_array_order/api/solvers/ortools.html\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.py at master · CPMpy/cpmpy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy/blob/master/cpmpy/solvers/ortools.py\"},{\"title\":\"Generating Special-Purpose Stateless Propagators for Arbitrary Constraints | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-15396-9_19\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - CPMpy/cpmpy: Constraint Programming and Modeling library in Python, based on numpy, with direct solver access. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy\"},{\"title\":\"cpmpy/docs/multiple_solutions.md at master · CPMpy/cpmpy\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/CPMpy/cpmpy/blob/master/docs/multiple_solutions.md\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found information about CPMpy's approach to custom constraints and callbacks. Here's what I found:\n\n## CPMpy Custom Constraints and Callbacks\n\nA DirectConstraint is a CPMpy expression so it can be part of a model like any other CPMpy constraint. The DirectConstraint, when used, calls a function on the ort_model object. Note that it can only be used as top-level (non-nested, non-reified) constraint.\n\n### Solution Callbacks\n\nFor solution callbacks, CPMpy supports solution tracking during solving. The or-tools interface supports solution_callback: an ort.CpSolverSolutionCallback object. CPMpy includes its own, namely OrtSolutionCounter.\n\nAdditionally, CPMpy passes arguments to solve() directly to the underlying solver object, so you can actually define your own native callbacks and pass them to the solve call. The following is an example of that, which is actually how the native solveAll() for OR-Tools is implemented.\n\nThe documentation also notes that for a complete list of global constraints, their meaning and more information on how to define your own, see the API documentation on global constraints.\n\nFor more detailed information on implementing custom propagators or constraints, you may want to check the official CPMpy API documentation on global constraints.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ab01e82d-db13-4d49-bd32-82474c733356","timestamp":"2026-05-09T23:37:40.317Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8875b875-bedd-49c1-91f2-072724160918","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/home/zhuran24/claude-pj/zmd","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.138","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
